  "extracted_text": "NHS Confidential: Personal Data About a Patient\nDate:\n22/04/2026\nNHS\nDocument:\nCardiology Clinic Letter\n27 APR 2026\nOxford University Hospitals\nPatient:\nNHS Foundation Trust\nDoB:\nMRN:\n11088659\nNHS:\nAddress:\n, 3 Hayley Green, BRACKNELL, RG42 3BT\nDepartment\nPaediatric Cardiology Department - Dr Bernadette Brent - Paediatric Cardiology Clinic\nChildren's Hospital, John Radcliffe Hospital\nDate seen: 20/04/2026.\nLetter status: Final.\nGP Letter\nDiagnosis (this visit)\nTGF-beta receptor 2 mutation\nFamily history of Loeys-Dietz Syndrome\nResults Review\nWeight 16.2kg, height 95cm\nDear Colleague\nIt was a pleasure to meet Alexis and her mum for a cardiac assessment as part of her review in the\ninherited aortopathy clinic. Alexis is now 21-month-old and she has inherited her mother's\nmutation in TGF-beta receptor 2. Mum told me that she and her dad had been followed up initially\nfor suspected Marfan's syndrome but she was then discharged as her genetics were negative.\nWhen she presented with a spinal fluid leak however full genome sequencing was done and she\nwas found to have Loeys-Dietz Syndrome and her dad was subsequently also found to have the\nmutation.\nAlexis is really well and thriving nicely with no cardiac symptoms.\nClinical examination revealed regular, good volume pulses and synchronous femorals. Auscultation\nrevealed normal heart sounds and no murmur.\nEcho was quite challenging as Alexis did not enjoy the experience. No ECG leads were placed. The\nchambers looked balanced and there was good biventricular function and no obvious valve\npathology. The aorta was not dilated, measuring 18.7mm at the sinuses (+0.84). The aortic arch was\nunobstructed. There was no obvious intracardiac shunt.\nI am pleased to report that Alexis heart looks normal at this stage. I explained we will continue to\nmonitor her progress and will attempt another full echo in 1 year's time in this clinic.\nNC0B0IVT000057020200\nCardiology Clinic Letter\n22/Apr/2026 14:02:32\n3 of 4\n\nNHS Confidential: Personal Data About a Patient\nMRN:11088659\nYours Sincerely,\nsigned electronically\nDr Bernadette Brent\nSpecialty Doctor in Paediatric Cardiology\nSwitch Board: 0300 304 7777\nSecretary Tel: 01865 231313\nSecretary Email: joy.demi@ouh.nhs.uk\nOutcome\nNext clinic visit.\nCopy to patient: Copy.\nCopies to OUH Staff sent internally via Message Centre:\nProfessor Tonia Vincent\nHonorary Consultant Rheumatologist\nProfessor of Musculoskeletal Biology\nCardiology Clinic Letter\n22/Apr/2026 14:02:32\n4 of 4",
