  "summaries": {
    "clinician": {
      "summary": "Patient alexis, a 21-month-old, was reviewed in the inherited aortopathy clinic. She has inherited a mutation in the TGF-beta receptor 2 gene, which is associated with Loeys-Dietz Syndrome. She is currently asymptomatic with a normal cardiovascular examination. Echocardiography showed a normal-sized aorta (18.7mm at the sinuses) and no valvular or structural cardiac abnormalities. Alexis will continue to be monitored in the paediatric cardiology clinic, with a repeat echocardiogram planned in 1 year's time",
      "confidence": 0.8
    },
    "patient": {
      "summary": "female patient was assessed for inherited heart and blood vessel conditions. She has inherited a genetic mutation from her mother which can affect the structure of the heart and blood vessels. However, the assessment found that at this stage, the patient's heart looks normal and is working well. The doctor will continue to monitor the patient's progress and will check her heart again in 1 year's time at the next clinic appointment",
      "confidence": 0.8
    },
    "pharmacist": {
      "summary": "No medications were documented in the provided clinical information. The patient, Alexis, was assessed in the paediatric cardiology clinic and was found to have a mutation in the TGF-beta receptor 2 gene associated with Loeys-Dietz Syndrome. The clinical examination and echocardiogram findings were reassuring, with no evidence of cardiac abnormalities at this stage. The patient was advised to have a follow-up echocardiogram in 1 year's time in the cardiology clinic.",
      "confidence": 0.8
